Hello everyone,<div><br></div><div>I have what I think is more of a coding question, but it&#39;s something I&#39;ve been banging my head against a wall about for awhile now so I thought I&#39;d just ask. I&#39;m following example 7.7 in &quot;Bayesian population analysis using WinBUGS&quot; along with the example in the recent &quot;

Zero-inflated count distributions for capture–mark–
reencounter data&quot; from Riecke et al. (2022). </div><div><br></div><div>I am currently trying to figure out how I can constrain survival differently for juveniles and adults. I&#39;m currently using an age matrix with nested indexing to account for the age structure, but I feel like this is causing problems when trying to incorporate different environemtnal covariates for the different age groups (but appears necessary for the curent CMR model structure). Currently I have the model set up to include random temporal effects,  but I&#39;d like to eventually be able to include <u>different</u> environmental covariates for the different age groups (with juveniles being ages 0-3 and adults being aged 4+). I&#39;m using only known-aged individuals in which exact age at marking is know. Any thoughts or suggestions about how to accomplish this would be grealty appreciated. I have the feeling it&#39;s an easy fix, I just can&#39;t seem to find to solution. Below I have pasted the pertinent parts of my code, happy to share some data if that would be helpful too. Cheers!</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>################ SELECTED CODE ################################</div><div><br></div><div>#Create age matrix covariate for known aged individuals<br># Age 4 = average age of return, using this as break for juveniles/adults</div><div># Juveniles ages 0-3, adults ages 4+</div><div><br>recode_ch &lt;- function(ch, f){<br>  z &lt;- ch<br>  for (i in 1:nrow(ch)) {<br>    for (j in 1:ncol(ch)) {<br>      if (j &lt; (f[i])){z[i,j] &lt;- NA}<br>      if (j == (f[i])){z[i,j] &lt;- 1}<br>      if (j == (f[i]+1)){z[i,j] &lt;- 1}<br>      if (j == (f[i]+2)){z[i,j] &lt;- 1}<br>      if (j &gt;= (f[i]+3)){z[i,j] &lt;- 1}<br>      if (j &gt;= (f[i]+4)){z[i,j] &lt;- 2}<br>    }<br>  }<br>  z &lt;- as.matrix(z)<br>  return(z)<br>}<br>age = recode_ch(j_ch,f.j)<br><br><br></div><div>###############################################################<br>CMR CODE<br>###############################################################<br><br># Write JAGS model file<br>cat(file=&quot;ATPU_ZIGP.txt&quot;, &quot;<br>model { <br># Priors and constraints<br>for (i in 1:nind){<br>   for (t in f[i]:(n.occasions-1)){<br>      logit(phi[i,t]) &lt;- alpha[age[i,t]] + eps[age[i,t],t] # Constrain survival to be age-specific<br>      } #t<br>   } #i<br>   <br><br>for (u in 1:2){<br>   alpha[u] ~ dunif(0, 10)       # Priors for age and time specific survival<br>   }<br><br><br>for (t in 1:(n.occasions-1)){<br>for (u in 1:2){<br>  eps[u,t] ~ dnorm(0,tau)<br>  }<br>}<br><br><br># More priors<br> <br>  epsilon ~ dgamma(1,1) # Prior for mean expected # encounters per individual<br>  gamma[1] ~ dbeta(1, 1)  # Prior for probability of availablity at time t given absense at time t-1<br>  gamma[2] ~ dbeta(1, 1) # Prior for probability of availablity at time t given available at time t-1<br>  sigma ~ dunif(0.5, 100)<br>  tau &lt;- pow(sigma, -2)<br><br>  <br> # Take inverse logit to backtransform survival probabilities<br>for (t in 1:(n.occasions-1)){<br>     phi.j[t] &lt;- 1 / (1+exp(-alpha[1]-eps[1,t]))<br>     phi.a[t] &lt;- 1 / (1+exp(-alpha[2]-eps[2,t]))<br>   }<br><br><br>###############################################################<br>CJS model <br>###############################################################<br># Capture-recapture data (CJS model with multinomial likelihood)<br># Define the multinomial likelihood<br><br># CMR Model Likelihood components<br>for (i in 1:nind){<br><br>   for (t in (f[i]+1):n.occasions){<br>   <br>      z[i,t] ~ dbern(phi[i,t-1] * z[i,t-1])<br>   <br>      # State process<br>      a[i,t] ~ dbern(mu1[i,t])<br>      mu1[i,t] &lt;- z[i,t] * gamma[a[i,t-1]+1]<br>      <br>      # Observation process<br>      c[i,t] ~ dpois(mu2[i,t])<br>      mu2[i,t] &lt;- a[i,t] * epsilon <br>      } #t<br>   } #i<br><br>} # end model<br><br>&quot;)<br><br><br><br><br># Parameters monitored<br>parameters &lt;- c(&quot;alpha&quot;,&quot;gamma&quot;,&quot;phi.j&quot;,&quot;phi.a&quot;, &quot;epsilon&quot;)<br><br><br><br>inits &lt;- function(){list(alpha = runif(2, 0, 1), <br>                         sigma = runif(1, 0.1, 10))}<br><br><br>ATPU_ZIGP_data &lt;- list(z = z.dat, <br>                       a = a.dat, <br>                       f = f,<br>                       nind = dim(ch)[1], <br>                       n.occasions = dim(ch)[2],<br>                       c=c,<br>                       age=age)</div><div>  <br># MCMC settings<br>ni &lt;- 500000; nb &lt;- 100000; nc &lt;- 3; nt &lt;- 3; na &lt;- 5000<br><br># Call JAGS<br>ATPU_ZIGP_out &lt;- jags(ATPU_ZIGP_data, inits=inits, parameters, &quot;ATPU_ZIGP.txt&quot;, n.iter=ni, n.burnin=nb, n.chains=nc, n.thin=nt, n.adapt=na, parallel = TRUE)<br></div><div><br></div><div>####################### END CODE ################################</div><div><br></div>
